// Fix round 2 regression pin: a producer group write (four `_m`
// selector stores sharing one base node and one whole-vector value)
// followed by ANY fifth consecutive matching-shape element store
// cannot fall back to elementwise lowering -- each store's whole-
// vector value would print into one scalar component target -- so the
// four-component count cap keeps the loud unsupported-operation
// failure for producer-marked runs.  The trailing store is spelled as
// a single `_m` selector write: selector targets carry CG_SCALAR_INT
// coordinates and match the recognizer shape, unlike explicit [r][c]
// chains whose folded constants are CG_SCALAR_CINT.  Expected: error
// C6201 at the entry ("GLSL profile program"), no output published.

void main(float4 position : POSITION,
          out float4 clip : POSITION)
{
    float4x4 local;

    clip = position;
    local._m00_m11_m22_m33 = position;
    local._m01 = position.w;
    clip.y += local[0][0] + local[0][1];
}
